OL,3,GNEWSALandslip repair funding decision
OL,4,Ais 'imminent'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA funding decision to rebuild a road
OL,7,Fdevastated by a huge landslip more than
OL,8,Fthree years ago is "imminent",
OL,9,Faccording to official papers.
OL,11,FThe A226 Galley Hill Road in Swanscombe
OL,12,Fhas been shut since 2023 when a chalk
OL,13,Fcliff collapsed on to neighbouring
OL,14,Findustrial estate following a burst
OL,15,Fwater main.
OL,17,FSince then, efforts have been made to
OL,18,Ffind a solution, the cost of which Kent
OL,19,FCounty Council (KCC) previously
OL,20,Festimated as being in excess of #40m.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
